---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

import Site from '@/layouts/Site.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '@/components/ui/Breadcrumb.astro';
import Button from '@/components/ui/Button.astro';
import JsonLd from '@/components/ui/JsonLd.astro';
import Icon from '@/components/marketing/Icon.astro';

import farmTrackGate from '@/assets/images/farm-track-gate.jpg';
import riverValleyAerial from '@/assets/images/river-valley-aerial.jpg';
import { buildShareImage } from '@/lib/metadata/share-image';
import { contactUrl, postUrl } from '@/lib/urls';

const share = await buildShareImage(farmTrackGate);
---

<Site
  title="The Property - Carinya Parc"
  description="42 hectares at The Branch, near Stroud, in the Upper Hunter. River plantings, a first food forest, new fences, five dams, and the shed we live in."
  path="/about/the-property"
  image={share.src}
  imageWidth={share.width}
  imageHeight={share.height}
  imageAlt="A gate onto the farm track"
>
  <JsonLd />

  <div class="isolate min-h-screen bg-paperbark">
    {/* Breadcrumb navigation */}
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1240px] px-6 pt-8 lg:px-14">
      <Breadcrumb />
    </div>

    <div class="relative isolate overflow-hidden py-16 sm:py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1240px] lg:flex lg:justify-between lg:px-14 xl:justify-end">
        <div class="lg:flex lg:w-1/2 lg:shrink lg:grow-0 xl:absolute xl:inset-y-0 xl:right-1/2 xl:w-1/2">
          <div class="relative h-80 lg:-ml-8 lg:h-auto lg:w-full lg:grow xl:ml-0">
            <Image
              src={riverValleyAerial}
              alt="Aerial view of Carinya Parc property"
              widths={[640, 1080, 1600]}
              sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 50vw"
              quality={80}
              loading="eager"
              fetchpriority="high"
              decoding="sync"
              class="absolute inset-0 size-full bg-line/40 object-cover"
            />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="px-6 lg:contents">
          <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl pt-16 pb-24 sm:pt-20 sm:pb-32 lg:mr-0 lg:ml-8 lg:w-full lg:max-w-lg lg:flex-none lg:pt-32 xl:w-1/2">
            <p class="text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-bracken-500">
              Our Land
            </p>
            <h1 class="mt-3.5 font-heading text-4xl font-normal tracking-tight text-pretty text-eucalypt-600 sm:text-5xl">
              The Property
            </h1>
            <p class="mt-6 text-xl/8 text-charcoal">
              Carinya Parc is 42 hectares at The Branch, near Stroud, in the Upper Hunter, NSW.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-10 max-w-xl text-base/7 text-charcoal lg:max-w-none">
              <p>
                The land runs for more than 400 metres along the Branch River, from a frost-free
                ridge down to a valley flat. It was an alpaca farm until early 2024. We rested the
                paddocks for two summers. Since then the work is trees, fences, water we have
                walked, and a shed we live in.
              </p>
              <ul role="list" class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-charcoal">
                <li class="flex gap-x-3">
                  <Icon name="map-pin" class="mt-1 size-5 flex-none text-eucalypt-600" />
                  <span>
                    Located at The Branch, near Stroud, in the Upper Hunter, NSW, 5 km from Stroud,
                    70 km to Newcastle, and within easy reach of Barrington Tops National Park, Port
                    Stephens, and the Great Lakes region.
                  </span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-x-3">
                  <Icon name="clock" class="mt-1 size-5 flex-none text-eucalypt-600" />
                  <span>
                    Alpacas came off in early 2024. Two summers of rest followed. We moved here
                    full-time in June 2026.
                  </span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-x-3">
                  <Icon name="droplets" class="mt-1 size-5 flex-none text-eucalypt-600" />
                  <span>
                    Five farm dams, four troughs, and a gravity line from the top dam. The homestead
                    dam is spring-fed. Along the river we are planting the bank the flood took.
                  </span>
                </li>
              </ul>
              <h2 class="mt-16 font-heading text-2xl font-normal tracking-tight text-eucalypt-600">
                What is in the ground
              </h2>
              <p class="mt-6">
                In April 2026, 26 people planted 1,150 native trees along 200 metres of the bend. In
                September we planted the first three food-forest rows on the slope below the
                homestead: 90 metres, about 380 plants. The long job is still 30,000 trees.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-6">
                Over the winter of 2026 we built 1.4 kilometres of fence: 740 metres on the eastern
                boundary and 660 metres of electric line on the north ridge. The western boundary
                and the river frontage are still the old alpaca wire. Cattle are planned for autumn
                2027. None are here yet.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-6">
                We live in the Colorbond shed, 15 metres by 9, and we are lining it while we live in
                it. The homestead cottage stays for guests. Stays are still to come. A visit today
                is by appointment: a planting day or a small-group tour.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-6">
                The working is in the journal:
                <a
                  href={postUrl('two-summers-of-rest')}
                  class="font-semibold text-eucalypt-600 hover:opacity-70"
                >
                  two summers of rest
                </a>
                ,
                <a
                  href={postUrl('first-planting-day')}
                  class="font-semibold text-eucalypt-600 hover:opacity-70"
                >
                  the first planting day
                </a>
                ,
                <a
                  href={postUrl('first-syntropic-lines')}
                  class="font-semibold text-eucalypt-600 hover:opacity-70"
                >
                  the first syntropic lines
                </a>
                ,
                <a
                  href={postUrl('old-fences-new-lines')}
                  class="font-semibold text-eucalypt-600 hover:opacity-70"
                >
                  the winter fences
                </a>
                ,
                <a
                  href={postUrl('five-dams-one-hot-week')}
                  class="font-semibold text-eucalypt-600 hover:opacity-70"
                >
                  the dams
                </a>
                , and
                <a
                  href={postUrl('the-shed-in-winter')}
                  class="font-semibold text-eucalypt-600 hover:opacity-70"
                >
                  living in the shed
                </a>
                .
              </p>
              <div class="mt-10 flex items-center gap-x-6">
                <Button href="/regenerate/" variant="bracken">
                  Get involved
                </Button>
                <a
                  href={contactUrl('tours')}
                  class="text-sm font-semibold leading-6 text-eucalypt-600 hover:opacity-70"
                >
                  <span>
                    Ask about a tour <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                  </span>
                </a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Site>
